spec:
  id: memory_updates
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: highest
  module: Cognition
  compiler_stage: Memory Evolution
  description: >
purpose[6]: Update,consolidate,reinforce,reorganize,preserve,engineering memory.
philosophy[6]: Memory evolves.,Knowledge never remains static.,Better evidence updates memory.,History is preserved.,"Learning changes memory,",not history.
pipeline[15]: Experience,→,Reflection,→,Lesson,→,Memory Lookup,→,Conflict Detection,→,Update Strategy,→,Validation,→,Graph Update
inputs[8]: Engineering Knowledge Record,Knowledge Atom,Reflection,Decision,Failure,Benchmark,Production Incident,User Feedback
outputs[5]: Updated Memory,New Memory,Merged Memory,Archived Memory,Revised Memory
operations[8]: Create,Reinforce,Modify,Merge,Split,Replace,Archive,Deprecate
create[5]: New Concept,New Pattern,New Failure,New Heuristic,New Capability
reinforce[4]: Repeated Success,Independent Validation,Production Success,Multiple Sources
modify[4]: Better Evidence,Improved Explanation,Updated Constraint,New Tradeoff
merge[4]: Duplicate Memories,Similar Lessons,Related Concepts,Equivalent Patterns
split[3]: Overgeneralized Memory,Multiple Independent Concepts,Mixed Failure Modes
replace[4]: Incorrect Model,Deprecated Practice,Superior Algorithm,Better Architecture
archive[3]: Legacy Knowledge,Deprecated Technology,Obsolete Practices
conflicts[4]: Contradictory Evidence,Duplicate Identity,Invalid Assumptions,Incompatible Versions
resolution[4]: Prefer Stronger Evidence,Prefer Production Validation,Preserve Older Version,Escalate Conflict
consolidation[5]: Compress,Link,Generalize,Specialize,Cross Reference
graph[5]: Add Node,Remove Edge,Create Edge,Update Weight,Update Confidence
versioning[4]: Immutable History,Incremental Versions,Parent References,Lineage Preservation
confidence[4]: Increase,Decrease,Propagate,Recalculate
learning[4]: Reinforce Capabilities,Update Mental Models,Improve Heuristics,Correct Misconceptions
ekr[3]: Every Engineering Knowledge Record,generates one or more,Memory Update Operations.
validation[4]: Every update has evidence.,Every modification preserves history.,Every replacement records rationale.,Every merge maintains provenance.
examples:
  Example_01:
    description: "Previous Memory: Global Lock New Lesson: Fine Grained Locking"
    Operation: Replace
  Example_02:
    description: "Repeated Incidents: Database Timeout"
    Operation: Reinforce
  Example_03:
    description: "Similar Lessons: Retry Strategy Exponential Backoff"
    Operation: Merge
  Example_04:
    description: New Production Evidence
    Operation: Increase Confidence
metrics[6]: Memory Growth,Reinforcement Rate,Merge Rate,Conflict Rate,Replacement Rate,Knowledge Density
success[6]: Engineering memory,continuously evolves,while preserving,"provenance,",correctness,and historical context.
guarantees[5]: Immutable History,Continuous Evolution,Provenance Preservation,Evidence Based Updates,Graph Consistency
future:
  autonomous_memory_optimization: true
  semantic_memory_compression: true
  graph_reorganization: true
  adaptive_memory_priorities: true
  lifelong_memory_growth: true
